WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.360
Learn to describe and represent decimals (tenths and hundredths) concretely,

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:08.520
pictorially, and symbolically and round decimals to the nearest tenth

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:18.609
0 tenths and 7 hundredths make which decimal? The answer is 0.07. 0/10 plus 7/100

00:00:18.609 --> 00:00:19.841
equals 0.07.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:25.711
A ruler reading has 3 tenths and 8 hundredths of a metre. What decimal length is

00:00:25.711 --> 00:00:28.529
this? Pause and solve it in your exercise book.

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:35.852
The answer is 0.38. 3/10 plus 8/100 equals 0.38.
